{"name":"Tangara","hex":"#97725f","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tangara","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Thraupidae – typical tanagers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tangara"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tangara (bird)","blocks":[{"text":"Tangara  is a large genus of birds of the tanager family. It includes 27 species. All are from the Neotropics, and while most are fairly widespread, some have small distributions and are threatened. They are fairly small, ranging in size from 11.5–15 centimetres (4.5–5.9 in). This genus includes some of the most spectacularly colored birds of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Flame-faced_Tanager_%28Tangara_parzudakii_lunigera%29.jpg/330px-Flame-faced_Tanager_%28Tangara_parzudakii_lunigera%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tangara_(bird)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Flame-faced_Tanager_%28Tangara_parzudakii_lunigera%29.jpg/500px-Flame-faced_Tanager_%28Tangara_parzudakii_lunigera%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Flame-faced_Tanager_%28Tangara_parzudakii_lunigera%29.jpg/1280px-Flame-faced_Tanager_%28Tangara_parzudakii_lunigera%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Flame-faced_Tanager_%28Tangara_parzudakii_lunigera%29.jpg/500px-Flame-faced_Tanager_%28Tangara_parzudakii_lunigera%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlame-faced_Tanager_(Tangara_parzudakii_lunigera).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Tangara_vassorii_by_Francesco